Later in the afternoon, I walk over to Eva's desk.
She is the team's digital designer.
I have not worked with her before today.
"Hi Maya, come and look," she says.
She points at her large screen.
I see some beautiful sketches of our new software.
The colors are calm, and the design is very clean.
"That looks really good," I say.
"Thank you," Eva answers with a smile.
She explains her work to me.
"I have worked as a digital designer since university," she says.
"I always focus on the user's experience."
She shows me how the user clicks around the program.
"It must be easy and logical to use," she explains.
I often only look at the code itself.
But her design is incredibly important for the project.
We talk a little more about our shared tasks.
I look forward to programming her beautiful design.
